Create a cohesive family of reusable Urkaaaz gold button backgrounds, based
on the approved Loadout `START MATCH` button design. Use the same visual
family for all button roles, including compact navigation such as `BACK`.
Generate five sizes and two interaction states for each size.

## Reference

- Attach the Loadout screenshot showing the Start Match button as the primary
  reference for its wide gold silhouette, bevels, decorative side details,
  contrast, and placement.
- Attach the approved `loadout_start_match_button_normal.png` and
  `loadout_start_match_button_pressed.png` as the definitive shape and state
  references. Preserve their design rather than inventing a new button style.
- Use approved Urkaaaz Loadout panels and buttons as secondary references for
  metal, wood, lighting, and finish.
- Match the existing Urkaaaz visual language: polished fantasy-game
  craftsmanship, strong gold face, darker bronze bevels, and restrained
  highlights. Do not copy unrelated screen content.

## Output

- Generate exactly ten separate transparent PNG files: one normal and one
  pressed asset for each size in the table below.
- All canvases are RGBA PNGs with a 4:1 aspect ratio. The pixel dimensions
  are 4x the target display dimensions; the UI will render each asset at its
  corresponding dp size.

| Size | Target display size | PNG canvas size |
|---|---:|---:|
| XS | 128 x 32 dp | 512 x 128 px |
| S | 176 x 44 dp | 704 x 176 px |
| M | 220 x 55 dp | 880 x 220 px |
| L | 280 x 70 dp | 1120 x 280 px |
| XL | 360 x 90 dp | 1440 x 360 px |

- The M size is the reference size and closely matches the current 220 x 54 dp
  Loadout button.
- Use these exact filenames:
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xs_normal.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xs_pressed.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_s_normal.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_s_pressed.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_m_normal.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_m_pressed.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_l_normal.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_l_pressed.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xl_normal.png`
  - `loadout_start_match_button_xl_pressed.png`
- Save all ten files for review under `assets_src/loadout/ui/`.
- Keep the outer silhouette, gold palette, bevels, ornament positions, and
  center text safe area consistent across all ten files. Within each size,
  the normal and pressed states must be pixel-aligned in geometry.
- These are background assets only. Do not copy them into Android resources
  until the user approves the preview.

## Shared design

- Create a broad, landscape-oriented button plate with a luminous warm-gold
  face, a substantial darker bronze/gold bevel, and a clear edge against the
  dark Loadout footer.
- Use a refined fantasy-game finish with controlled highlights and subtle
  dimensionality. The button should feel important and tappable without
  overpowering the rest of the Loadout screen.
- Keep the same gold face, bevel, silhouette language, and state treatment for
  primary, secondary, and navigation buttons. Do not create a separate plain,
  silver, blue, or text-only button style for `BACK`.
- The XS background is intended for compact controls such as `BACK`. Its
  plate may be wider than the former text-only Back label; that is deliberate
  so the control belongs to the same button family. Render the live label
  centered on the plate.
- Small symmetrical diamond, rivet, or carved-metal accents may frame the
  far left and right sides. Keep them outside the center text safe area.
- Keep the central face spacious, simple, and evenly lit so Android can draw
  the live `START MATCH` label over it with strong contrast.
- Use transparent pixels outside the button silhouette. Keep even safety
  margins so the plate can be scaled to the existing wide button proportion
  without clipping its corners or glow.
- The M background must remain legible at the existing approximate
  220 x 54 dp button size.
- Adjust proportions and detail density for each target size without changing
  the shared design. Keep the central text-safe area proportional and large
  enough for a short live button label.
- Keep the XS artwork simple enough to remain crisp at 128 x 32 dp. The app
  should provide an accessible touch target separately if that visual size is
  used for an interactive control.

## Unpressed assets

- Make the gold face bright, inviting, and clearly raised above the footer.
- Show a crisp upper bevel, warm gold highlights, and a restrained outer
  highlight or glow.
- Keep the silhouette and center text area calm; avoid reflections that could
  reduce the readability of the live label.

## Pressed assets

- For every size, preserve the exact geometry and ornament placement of its
  matching unpressed asset.
- Make the face look physically pressed inward: reduce the raised bevel and
  outer glow, slightly deepen the gold/bronze shadows, and lower or compress
  the inner face subtly while preserving the outer bounds.
- Keep the pressed state clearly distinguishable at a glance, but retain
  enough gold brightness and contrast to read as the same enabled action.
- Do not make it red, disabled, broken, selected, or permanently depressed.

## Runtime separation

- Do not include `START MATCH`, letters, numbers, icons, arrows, labels,
  watermark, signature, or any other text in any PNG.
- Android renders live button labels separately and switches between the
  matching size's normal and pressed assets.
- Render live labels in Cinzel SemiBold with a dark, high-contrast color on
  the gold face.
- Do not add a disabled-state asset, loading indicator, spinner, or extra
  action; those are outside this ten-file request.
- Do not flatten the footer or any other UI into either button background.

## Negative prompt

text, letters, numbers, words, logo, watermark, signature, opaque background,
full-screen UI, screenshot, phone frame, rectangular image backdrop, card
frame, overly ornate scrollwork, tiny unreadable details, asymmetrical
ornaments, different geometry between states, clipped bevel, excessive bloom,
red pressed state, disabled state, loading state, extra icon, extra button

## Review checklist

- Confirm there are exactly ten PNG files with the specified filenames and
  exact dimensions.
- Confirm all files are RGBA with transparency outside the button silhouette.
- Compare each normal/pressed pair as an overlay: geometry and ornament
  placement should align exactly.
- Confirm all five sizes form one consistent family and that larger sizes do
  not introduce extra decoration or different button proportions.
- Confirm each pressed state is visibly lower and less luminous while
  remaining clearly enabled.
- Review each size at its target dp dimensions against the dark Loadout
  footer, including the central live-text area.
- Show all five normal/pressed pairs individually for review before Android
  integration.
